{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Plague","id":"476553068687654922","is_bot":0,"username":"__plague"},"author_id":"476553068687654922","channel_id":"854826651169587252","content":"It's getting kind of late. They're not sure why, but Mictlan sort of likes it here. It's calming without the really kind of off-putting thing that's weird in a way that Mictlan isn't on the, er, island? Geography is kind of difficult when leylines and stuff happen.\n\nIt's. Er. It's nice. They know they'll be kind of hopeless with nature magic forever even if they're smart, but that's okay. The plants generally don't judge very much and they do stay alive (though they're not entirely sure if it's because they're here or that they're just not killing the plants). Though someone would probably mention if Mictlan was blazing a giant path of destruction through all greenery they touched, ever. \n\nHmm. \n\nThey sing, a little, as they go around taking off dying leaves and flowers and checking the soil and stuff. It sounds a bit eldritch and a little celestial and it probably isn't very musical for anyone who hears, but they can sort of carry a tune. Or maybe it's just that they remember things more fondly. Mictlan cares, a little, then they don't, because their life is short enough not to have to spend time wondering about the perceptions of... people, they guess. It's nice, sort of but entirely different from the way a library is.","created_at":"2021-07-26T06:51:14.239000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"869109592968282133","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
